---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="San Francisco Pedestrian Injuries Attorney | The Sulfab Law Office"
  description="Hit by a vehicle while walking in San Francisco? Sulfab Law Office helps pedestrian accident victims recover compensation. Call (415) 360-5266."
  canonical="/pedestrian-injuries-lawyer-san-francisco/"
>
  <section class="relative bg-dark pt-28 pb-32 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-br from-dark via-dark to-slate-900/80"></div>
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-16 relative z-10">
      <div class="max-w-4xl">
        <div class="w-16 h-1 bg-gold rounded-full mb-8"></div>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-gold text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.4em] mb-6">Personal Injury</span>
        <h1 class="text-white text-5xl md:text-7xl font-bold leading-[1.05] tracking-tight mb-6">San Francisco Pedestrian Injuries Lawyer</h1>
        <p class="text-slate-400 text-xl md:text-2xl max-w-2xl leading-relaxed mb-10">Pedestrians have no protection against the force of a vehicle, making collisions especially dangerous. If you have been hit by a car, truck, or other vehicle while walking, our legal team is here to help you pursue the compensation you need.</p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
          <a href="tel:+14153605266" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-3 px-8 py-4 bg-gold text-white font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-xs hover:bg-amber-600 transition-all rounded-lg">Call (415) 360-5266</a>
          <a href="/#contact" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-3 px-8 py-4 border-2 border-white/25 text-white hover:border-gold hover:bg-white/5 transition-all rounded-lg">Free Case Review</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-20 bg-gradient-to-b from-white to-slate-50/50">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-16">
      <p class="text-slate-600 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">Pedestrian accidents are among the most serious types of traffic collisions. Unlike occupants of a vehicle, pedestrians have nothing to shield them from the impact, which means injuries are frequently catastrophic. San Francisco's dense urban environment, heavy traffic, and high volume of foot traffic create conditions where pedestrian accidents are tragically common. Crosswalks, intersections, and parking lots are all potential danger zones.</p>
      <p class="text-slate-600 text-lg leading-relaxed">At The Sulfab Law Office, we are committed to helping pedestrian accident victims and their families obtain the compensation they deserve. Our San Francisco pedestrian injury attorney understands the unique legal issues that arise in these cases, including disputes over right-of-way, driver visibility, and crosswalk laws. We conduct thorough investigations to determine liability and build strong cases that hold negligent drivers accountable for the harm they cause.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 md:py-20 border-t border-slate-100 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-16">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[5fr_7fr] gap-16 items-start">
        <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-28">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-gold text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.4em] mb-6">Experience Matters</span>
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-dark mb-6 italic font-serif">Strong Advocacy for Pedestrian Accident Victims</h2>
          <div class="w-16 h-1 bg-gold rounded-full"></div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">Pedestrian accident cases require a careful analysis of the circumstances surrounding the collision. Our San Francisco pedestrian injury lawyer works with accident reconstruction experts to determine factors such as vehicle speed, driver reaction time, visibility conditions, and pedestrian positioning. We gather surveillance footage, witness statements, police reports, and cell phone records to establish exactly what happened and who was at fault.</p>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">Insurance companies frequently argue that pedestrians share fault for accidents, even when the driver was clearly negligent. We are prepared to counter these arguments with strong evidence and legal arguments that demonstrate the driver's responsibility for your injuries. Our goal is to secure compensation that covers your medical care, lost income, and the pain and suffering you have endured.</p>
          <div class="mt-8 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-amber-50/50 border border-gold/20">
            <p class="text-slate-700 font-medium">Our firm is dedicated to protecting the rights of pedestrians and ensuring that victims receive the full compensation they are entitled to when a driver's negligence causes serious injury.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-slate-50/50 border-t border-slate-100">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-16">
      <div class="text-center mb-12">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-gold text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.4em] mb-6">Common Causes</span>
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-dark mb-6 italic font-serif">Common Causes of Pedestrian Accidents</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 max-w-xl mx-auto">Pedestrian accidents are almost always preventable. They typically result from driver inattention, reckless behavior, or failure to obey traffic laws.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-100">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-red-50 text-red-600 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 font-bold text-sm">!</span>
          <span class="text-slate-700 text-sm font-medium">Distracted driving</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-100">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-red-50 text-red-600 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 font-bold text-sm">!</span>
          <span class="text-slate-700 text-sm font-medium">Texting while driving</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-100">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-red-50 text-red-600 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 font-bold text-sm">!</span>
          <span class="text-slate-700 text-sm font-medium">Speeding</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-100">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-red-50 text-red-600 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 font-bold text-sm">!</span>
          <span class="text-slate-700 text-sm font-medium">Driving under the influence</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-100">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-red-50 text-red-600 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 font-bold text-sm">!</span>
          <span class="text-slate-700 text-sm font-medium">Drug-impaired driving</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-100">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-red-50 text-red-600 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 font-bold text-sm">!</span>
          <span class="text-slate-700 text-sm font-medium">Failure to yield to pedestrians</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-100">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-red-50 text-red-600 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 font-bold text-sm">!</span>
          <span class="text-slate-700 text-sm font-medium">Running red lights and stop signs</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-100">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-red-50 text-red-600 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 font-bold text-sm">!</span>
          <span class="text-slate-700 text-sm font-medium">Reckless driving</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-100">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-red-50 text-red-600 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 font-bold text-sm">!</span>
          <span class="text-slate-700 text-sm font-medium">Fatigued driving</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-100">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-red-50 text-red-600 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 font-bold text-sm">!</span>
          <span class="text-slate-700 text-sm font-medium">Poor visibility conditions</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-100">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-red-50 text-red-600 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 font-bold text-sm">!</span>
          <span class="text-slate-700 text-sm font-medium">Backing-up accidents</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 rounded-xl bg-white border border-slate-100">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-red-50 text-red-600 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 font-bold text-sm">!</span>
          <span class="text-slate-700 text-sm font-medium">Failure to obey traffic signals</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-white border-t border-slate-100">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-16">
      <div class="text-center mb-12">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-gold text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.4em] mb-6">Common Injuries</span>
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-dark mb-6 italic font-serif">Injuries From Pedestrian Accidents</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 max-w-xl mx-auto">Pedestrians are completely vulnerable to the force of a vehicle impact, often resulting in severe, life-changing injuries that require extensive medical treatment.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-slate-50/50 p-6 pl-8 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-slate-200 hover:border-gold transition-all">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-dark mb-3">Traumatic Brain Injuries</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">Head trauma from being struck by a vehicle frequently causes concussions, contusions, and severe brain damage. Cognitive impairment and long-term disability are serious concerns.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-50/50 p-6 pl-8 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-slate-200 hover:border-gold transition-all">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-dark mb-3">Spinal Cord Injuries</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">Impact from a vehicle can damage the spinal cord, leading to partial or complete paralysis. These injuries have devastating and permanent effects on mobility and quality of life.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-50/50 p-6 pl-8 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-slate-200 hover:border-gold transition-all">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-dark mb-3">Broken Bones and Fractures</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">Pedestrians struck by vehicles commonly suffer multiple fractures to the legs, arms, pelvis, and ribs. These injuries often require surgical intervention and lengthy rehabilitation.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-50/50 p-6 pl-8 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-slate-200 hover:border-gold transition-all">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-dark mb-3">Internal Injuries</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">Blunt force trauma from a vehicle can cause internal bleeding, organ damage, and other life-threatening conditions requiring emergency surgery and extended hospitalization.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-50/50 p-6 pl-8 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-slate-200 hover:border-gold transition-all">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-dark mb-3">Soft Tissue Injuries</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">Muscle, ligament, and tendon damage from a pedestrian accident can cause chronic pain, limited mobility, and long-term physical impairment requiring ongoing treatment.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-white border-t border-slate-100">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-16">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[5fr_7fr] gap-16 items-start">
        <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-28">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-gold text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.4em] mb-6">Legal Process</span>
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-dark mb-6 italic font-serif">Determining Liability in Pedestrian Accident Cases</h2>
          <div class="w-16 h-1 bg-gold rounded-full"></div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">Determining fault in a pedestrian accident requires a thorough investigation of multiple factors. Our legal team examines the driver's actions leading up to the collision, including whether they were distracted, speeding, or under the influence of drugs or alcohol. We also evaluate whether the pedestrian was in a marked crosswalk or intersection at the time of the accident, as this can significantly impact liability under California law.</p>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">In some cases, liability may extend beyond the driver. Government entities responsible for maintaining safe roadways and sidewalks may bear responsibility if poor lighting, missing signage, or dangerous road design contributed to the accident. Our firm identifies all potentially liable parties and pursues claims against each to maximize the compensation available to you.</p>
          <div class="mt-8 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-amber-50/50 border border-gold/20">
            <p class="text-slate-700 font-medium">If you have been injured in a pedestrian accident, it is important to seek legal guidance as soon as possible. Evidence can disappear quickly, and California's statute of limitations places strict deadlines on filing claims.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-slate-50/50 border-t border-slate-100">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-16">
      <div class="text-center mb-12">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-gold text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.4em] mb-6">Financial Recovery</span>
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-dark mb-6 italic font-serif">Compensation Available After a Pedestrian Accident</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto">Victims of pedestrian accidents caused by negligence may be entitled to compensation for a wide range of losses, both economic and non-economic.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="text-center p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-slate-100">
          <div class="inline-flex w-14 h-14 rounded-xl bg-amber-50 text-gold items-center justify-center mb-5">
            <svg class="w-7 h-7" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 2v20M17 5H9.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 0 7h5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7H6"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-dark mb-2">Medical Expenses</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">Coverage for emergency treatment, hospitalization, surgeries, medication, rehabilitation, and any future medical care related to your pedestrian accident injuries.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="text-center p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-slate-100">
          <div class="inline-flex w-14 h-14 rounded-xl bg-amber-50 text-gold items-center justify-center mb-5">
            <svg class="w-7 h-7" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-dark mb-2">Lost Wages and Earning Capacity</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">Compensation for time away from work, lost employment benefits, and diminished future earning capacity resulting from your injuries and ongoing recovery.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="text-center p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-slate-100">
          <div class="inline-flex w-14 h-14 rounded-xl bg-amber-50 text-gold items-center justify-center mb-5">
            <svg class="w-7 h-7" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-dark mb-2">Pain, Suffering and Other Damages</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">Compensation for physical pain, emotional distress, loss of enjoyment of life, and other non-economic damages caused by the pedestrian accident.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-20 bg-dark border-t border-slate-800">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-16 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-4 italic font-serif">Contact a Pedestrian Injury Lawyer in San Francisco Today</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-lg mb-10 max-w-2xl mx-auto">If you have been hit by a vehicle while walking in San Francisco, do not wait. Contact Sulfab Law Office today for a free consultation.</p>
      <a href="tel:+14153605266" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-3 px-8 py-4 bg-gold text-white font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-xs hover:bg-amber-600 transition-all rounded-lg">Call (415) 360-5266</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
